 "decisions": [
  {
   "what": "Open questions 1-8 answered as delegate (UART JST-GH 4p; 8-pin Hall+ABZ; 10 A RMS/20 A pk and 10-28 V PROVISIONAL; qty 5; top-side SMD; 4x M3)",
   "why": "Unattended run; brief says decide and journal; safety values re-confirmed at H1",
   "phase": "P0",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:04:41"
  },
  {
   "what": "Power stage uses 60 V FETs (2-3 mOhm, 5x6), not 40 V",
   "why": "VM TVS clamps ~45 V at 28 V standoff; 40 V FETs have no margin under clamp. Correctness over the brief's 40 V guess",
   "phase": "P1",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:08:55"
  },
  {
   "what": "No on-board fuse (external 20 A slow fuse required, stated in guide); no hot-swap inrush limit; no brake chopper - firmware limits regen on VM sense",
   "why": "Bench prototype; fuse/brake sized to the user's supply; recorded as PROVISIONAL safety answers for H1",
   "phase": "P1",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:08:56"
  },
  {
   "what": "Gate drive: DRV8300D on a 12 V GVDD boosted from 5 V (TPS61040), not DRV8320H's charge pump; overcurrent via CSA -> MCU comparators -> TIM1 break",
   "why": "DRV8320H guarantees only 6.3 V high-side VGS at VM=10 V, below the 8 V requirement",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:26:13"
  },
  {
   "what": "Key parts: NTMFS5C628NL 60 V FETs, LM5164 buck, INA240A1 G=20, STM32G431CBT6, LM74500 RP, SMCJ28A, 3 mOhm 2512 shunts, 4L JLC04162H-7628A 2 oz outer",
   "why": "architect P2; see architecture/blocks.md",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:26:14"
  },
  {
   "what": "Designing under coverage gap: tvs-clamp, boost, ldo, mcu, isns_a/b/c (no library checklist); buck gap is inrush only",
   "why": "Research cap and iteration spend: 4 of 6 research slots went to the safety-critical blocks (gate drive, half-bridge, shunt sensing, reverse-polarity FET). These are covered by P1 research (power.md, mcu.md, current-sense-amp.md) and will be checked against datasheet extraction at P3; buck inrush is bounded by the buck's own soft-start behind the RP-FET/bulk-cap path",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:32:51"
  },
  {
   "what": "Board renamed astra-motor -> bldc-motor-driver; spec is designed from a general brief; research found nothing about the reference board beyond the frame (research/reference-video.md)",
   "why": "Owner addenda 1790532180 / 1790532487: no Astra naming; research first, fall back to the frame-derived spec if nothing usable",
   "phase": "P0",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:32:51"
  },
  {
   "what": "research task block-half-bridge-inverter-1 closed over 1 unverified draft record(s): half-bridge-inverter-switch-node-damping",
   "why": "--accept-drafts: the slot ships without this knowledge",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:55:35"
  },
  {
   "what": "designing under coverage gap: all 12 P2 slots (power_in x2, regulators x3, gate_driver, power_stage, sensing, mcu, isns_a/b/c)",
   "why": "maturity floor is owner-approved; 19 verified research records (4 tasks) fold in only as provisional until promoted, switch-node-damping record refuted (10-48 V envelope unsupported, source is 5-21 V) and closed as draft; regulators/mcu/isns covered by P1 research md + P3 datasheet extraction; unattended run",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T14:56:30"
  },
  {
   "what": "designing under coverage gap at P3 exit: 9 topology/interface slots (tvs-clamp, buck, boost, ldo, half-bridge-inverter, mcu, isns_a/b/c) have no checklist; parts 8 covered/3 provisional",
   "why": "No new part-level gaps vs P2; hwde has no checklists for these topologies; the verified research records + datasheet extractions (8 ICs incl. STM32G431) carry the layout rules. Unattended run.",
   "phase": "P3",
   "ts": "2026-09-27T15:44:13"
  },
  {
   "what": "check_diffpair (ISNS_A/B/C): exit 1, 6 errors (skew 14.69/7.90/15.14 mm, N uncoupled 17.35/10.56/17.80 mm vs 3.0 mm limit) + 7 warnings (open_trunk x6: terminals are net ties; B via asymmetry). check_diffpair has no waiver input; the same 6 findings are waived in reports/verify-waivers.json and the verify gate records PASS.",
   "why": "Owner-approved: INA240 IN+ (pin 8) and IN- (pin 1) are on opposite pad rows 5.4 mm apart and the shunt Kelvin taps 3.46 mm apart, so ~9 mm uncoupled is set by the packages; INA240 has its own PWM rejection and the signal is low-frequency sense. A/C N legs loop round C511/C513; a B.Cu underpass would cut them to ~10.5 mm but add two vias and still fail, so left.",
   "phase": "P8",
   "ts": "2026-09-28T07:26:52"
  },
  {
   "what": "Fab package exported to fab/ (gerbers+drill zip, pos, BOM.csv, CPL.csv, prebuy.csv); BOM incomplete: 53 placed parts (sensing U501-503/C5xx/R5xx, io C70x/D70x/F70x/J70x/R70x) carry no LCSC number on the board and parts.json has no per-ref map. Not ordered.",
